# Per-link escapes for lychee, one why-comment per entry. The config itself
# (lychee.toml) is drift-audited template canon and must not gain carve-outs;
# this file is where a repo's own exceptions belong.

# The AGPL-3.0 text in LICENSES/ is verbatim by REUSE requirement — its header
# carries <https://fsf.org/>, and the apex name serves no usable TLS (the
# handshake fails outright; www.fsf.org is the host that answers). The text
# cannot be edited without breaking `reuse lint`, and the FSF's own TLS is not
# ours to fix, so the one link is excluded here. Re-test on any lychee bump:
# `curl -sSI https://fsf.org/` succeeding means this entry can go.
^https://fsf\.org/$
